    Improve Syntax Highlight

    Tags with a following dot ("."), initiate a text-context for writing, where
    new parsing rules apply until the space goes back one indentation level.

    Right now the CodeMirror syntax plugin does not account for this.

    I'm sure someone could challenge someone to vibe code the entire thing as a plugin
    for CodeMirror and I would gladly just use that.

    CodeMirror plugins are hot right now.

    ---
  
    Better syntax highlighting for the editor. More sensitive
    to the meaningful parts of the code.
    
    Should highlight the most meaningful parts.

    Should also adjust so it does not have an horizontal scroll bar.

    Or prettify automatically to fit within the current viewport.

    Each file could have it's own meta-tag about maximum width.

    Prettifycation of the code is currently done by Ctrl+S; it has
    some click sense to it; and it currenly it's only job is to lock to format
    the Style Declaration Brackets so that they are easier to parse by my own personal
    human preference.

    The prettification of the style declarations could be be adjusted depending on what you
